# CivicSOS environment variables.
#
# Copy to apps/web/.env.local for local development. Never commit a filled-in
# copy — .env.local is git-ignored for exactly this reason.
#
# Deployed values are NOT set here: Lambda's variables come from the CDK stack,
# and the frontend's come from Amplify's console. See DEPLOYMENT.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (public — these are embedded in the browser bundle by design)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Deployed API base URL, from the stack's ApiBaseUrl output.
# LEAVE UNSET for local development: the app then serves its own in-memory API
# running the identical router, services and rules as the deployed Lambda.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://abc123.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com

# Cognito, from the stack's UserPoolId / UserPoolClientId outputs.
# Both are public identifiers. Without them the app offers demo sessions only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=ap-south-1_XXXXXXXXX
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=1a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i0j

# The CivicSOS browser assistant's extension ID, shown by Chrome when you load
# apps/extension/dist unpacked. Comma-separate to allow more than one.
# An extension ID is public, not a secret. Leave unset and the app never offers
# the payload to any extension — it shows the copy-ready complaint instead,
# which is the path that works on every portal. See apps/extension/README.md.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSISTANT_EXTENSION_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side (SECRET — never prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Gemini free-tier key, for local development only.
# In a deployment this lives in SSM Parameter Store as a SecureString and is
# read by Lambda at cold start; it never reaches the browser.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey and do NOT enable billing.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Free-tier flash model. Override only if quotas change.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# HMAC secret for guest demo session tokens. At least 32 characters.
# Optional locally — one is generated per process if omitted — but setting it
# means demo sessions survive a dev-server restart.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\n=+/' | cut -c1-48
# GUEST_SESSION_SECRET=

# debug | info | warn | error
# LOG_LEVEL=info
